== ascription of a structure against a named module type
digest: checks 1 (ascription 1) deps 1 (interface 1) equalities 0 omissions 0
check ascription M : S ascription.ml:3:15-3:38
dep <M> -interface-> S
== the check is directional: only the implementation is checked
digest: checks 2 (ascription 2) deps 2 (interface 2) equalities 0 omissions 0
check ascription M : S directional.ml:4:15-4:38
check ascription N : T directional.ml:5:15-5:38
dep <M> -interface-> S
dep <N> -interface-> T
== aliases, includes, with constraints and module type of
digest: checks 4 (ascription 4) deps 12 (definition 3 alias 1 include 1 with 1 typeof 2 interface 4) equalities 0 omissions 0
check ascription M : S edges.ml:5:15-5:39
check ascription MA : A edges.ml:13:16-13:40
check ascription MW : W edges.ml:11:16-11:39
check ascription MK : K edges.ml:12:16-12:50
dep A -alias-> S
dep W -definition-> <#1>
dep G -definition-> <#2>
dep K -definition-> <#3>
dep <#1> -with-> S
dep <M> -interface-> S
dep <#2> -typeof-> S
dep <#2> -typeof-> <M>
dep <#3> -include-> S
dep <MW> -interface-> W
dep <MK> -interface-> K
dep <MA> -interface-> A
== composed destructive substitutions of types
digest: checks 1 (ascription 1) deps 7 (definition 2 include 2 with 2 interface 1) equalities 0 omissions 0
check ascription M : U subst.ml:10:15-10:38
dep T -definition-> <#1>
dep U -definition-> <#2>
dep <#1> -include-> S1
dep <#1> -include-> S2
dep <#3> -with-> T
dep <#2> -with-> <#3>
dep <M> -interface-> U
== destructive substitution of a module type
digest: checks 1 (ascription 1) deps 6 (definition 2 with 1 subst 1 interface 2) equalities 0 omissions 0
check ascription M : U mtsubst.ml:5:15-5:38
dep T -definition-> <#1>
dep U -definition-> <#2>
dep <#1> -interface-> T.X@body(T)
dep <#2> -subst-> S2
dep <#2> -with-> T
dep <M> -interface-> U
